Maritime Pack: KSP 1.12.5 NullReferenceException fixes, upstream patch set
==========================================================================

This file holds the changes for FOUR upstream code bases. Each section starts with a
"#### SECTION" banner naming the repository and the directory to apply it from
(all hunks use a/ b/ prefixes, so apply with -p1). Text outside diff hunks is commentary
and is ignored by `git apply` / GNU `patch`. To apply one section, copy it into its own
file first, using an editor or tool that keeps CR characters. The C# sources upstream use CRLF
line endings and the hunks keep them, so on Windows apply with `patch -p1 --binary < sectionN.diff`
or `git apply -p1 sectionN.diff`. Verified: with `patch -p1 --binary` every section applies
cleanly to its baseline and the result is byte-identical to src/. `git apply` produces the same
content, but with core.autocrlf=true it writes the LF-only files (section 4, the new .cfg) as CRLF.

Baselines used:
  1  Fengist/Maritime-Pack  GitHub zip snapshot 2822417 (GameData as shipped)
  2  Fengist/MPUtils        commit 40615d6 (2022-04-09); byte-identical to the shipped source,
                            and the shipped MPUtils.dll exposes the same API surface
  3  Fengist/MPHover        commit 6736813 (2018-07-30); MPHover.cs byte-identical to the baseline
  4  MPEngineSounds.dll and FengistAnim.dll as SHIPPED in the pack, decompiled with ILSpy.
     The public repos Fengist/MPEngineSounds (18733d8) and Fengist/Fengist-s-Animator
     (371e72d) are older than the shipped DLLs, so these hunks are against the decompiled
     source (in src/ of this release). Port them to the real sources by hand.

Build changes are not included as diffs. src/Directory.Build.props and the SDK-style
*.csproj files in this release build all four DLLs with `dotnet build -c Release` against
KSP 1.12.5 (net472, KSP/Unity references Private=false).

